    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d509">

                <pb facs="0620" n="1454" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v02/pg1454"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 656.119/348a</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in the
                        Netherlands</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Garrett</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-04-08T17:00:00-04:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 8, 1918, 5 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1085. Informed by Stevens that he has sent to you terms for chartering Dutch
                        ships,<anchor n="1" xml:id="d509-f1"/> which terms have been agreed to by
                    British Government, and that you are awaiting instructions from Department
                    before presenting these terms to Foreign Office. You may present terms, and give
                    wide publicity to them.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d509-f1" n="1" xml:id="d509-f1-content">
                <p>See telegram No. 6984, Mar. 21, to the Ambassador in Great Britain, <hi
                        rendition="#italic">ante</hi>, <ref target="#pg1423">p. 1423</ref>.</p>
            </note>
